{"kind":"stack","id":"s-forces","title":"Forces: contact and magnets","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#1f2d3d","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c1-p","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Which force needs the two objects to touch?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Pushing a ball with your foot","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"A magnet pulling a paperclip across the table","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Gravity pulling an apple down","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"A magnet pulls a paperclip without touching it. What kind of force is this?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"A contact force","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"A non-contact force","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"A friction force only","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-t","content":"Contact force"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-e","content":"A force that only works when the two objects are touching, such as pushing or kicking."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which of these is a contact force?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"A magnet attracting a nail","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Rubbing your hands together to slide them","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Gravity holding the moon in orbit","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You find a box with a magnet inside. Do you open it or shake it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Hold the magnet near a paperclip","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Shake the box to hear what rattles","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The paperclip jumps towards the magnet before you touch it. A non-contact force at work!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You hear a rattle. You must touch the box to feel what moves inside."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"A magnet can pull a pin from a short distance away. What is this called?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"A contact force","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"A non-contact force","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Air resistance","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Magnetic force"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"A force a magnet can exert on certain metals, even when they are not touching it."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which material would a magnet pull towards it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Wood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Plastic","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Iron","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"Well done! You finished the forces lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Contact forces need touching. Magnetic forces can act at a distance. Keep exploring!"}],"actions":[]}}
